#!/usr/bin/python3
"""
screen-ruler — a PowerToys Screen Ruler port for Ubuntu (GNOME, X11 and Wayland).

How it works (mirrors microsoft/PowerToys src/modules/MeasureTool):
  1. Take one snapshot of the desktop (PowerToys' default "non-continuous" mode).
  2. Show a borderless fullscreen overlay on every monitor, painted with that snapshot.
  3. On every pointer move, walk left/right/up/down from the pointer pixel until a
     pixel differs from the start pixel by more than the tolerance (EdgeDetection.cpp).
  4. Draw the measured lines/box and a label; click copies the size to the clipboard.

Modes: 1 Bounds  2 Spacing (cross)  3 Horizontal  4 Vertical   (Ctrl+1..4 also work)
Mouse:  click = copy & close · Shift+click = pin & keep going · wheel = tolerance ±15
Keys:   Esc / right click = close · +/- = tolerance · U = cycle extra unit
"""

from __future__ import annotations

